        "facts": ["The Sun's energy drives evaporation.", "Plants release water vapor by transpiration.", "Cooling air makes vapor condense into clouds.", "Gravity drives precipitation and the flow of water downhill."],
        "misconceptions": ["Clouds are made of water vapor rather than droplets or ice.", "Evaporation only happens from the oceans."] },
      { "key": "reservoirs", "title": "Describe where Earth's water is stored", "description": "Gives rough proportions of salt water, ice and groundwater and contrasts residence times.",
